      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Eastern Wastes [ToV]\n**Who:**\n- Essedera - CoV [ _Raids and Mission_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 112\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 05:08:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Chaos Infused Velium Shard [item=140285]\n- Fire Infused Velium Shard [item=140312]\n- Frost Infused Velium Shard [item=140270]\n- Lightning Infused Velium Shard [item=140288]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Sleeper's Tomb [CoV]: The Call (Group)\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Cargalia - CoV [npc=56362]\n- Honvar - CoV [npc=56366]\n- Melalafen - CoV [npc=56363]\n- Sivar - CoV [npc=56365]\n- Vulak`Aerr - CoV [npc=56364]\n- a bulky chest - CoV [npc=56449]\n- a confused caretaker - CoV [npc=56456]\n- a slimy golem - CoV [npc=56460]\n**Era:** | !Claws of Veeshan\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Oct 30 02:00:37 2020\nModified: Sun Aug 25 16:08:40 2024 | | **Claws of Veeshan Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**Prerequisite Quests:** None.\nYou can obtain this mission from Essedera [npc=56441] in The Eastern Wastes (ToV). You can find her at near the sleeper's tomb area. She is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Essedera'\nEssedera says, 'Well, Minasu, you must be one of those adventurers.' The drake \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* its head and leans toward you. 'What is it that you wish of me? Never mind, there is no longer a need to be coy, nor is there time for it. If you have come here to, um, [visit] with Vulak'Aerr, I can assist you. If not, then you should be on your way.'\nYou say, 'visit'\nEssedera says, 'Under any other circumstance I would object and offer you no assistance at all. But times are different at the moment, and one must do what needs to be done, no matter the consequences. If you come with a [small] group I can easily assist you on entry to the tomb. If you bring a [larger] group I will assist you, but it will be challenging to my magic.'\nYou say, 'small'\nEssedera says, 'So be it. This is a sad day for me and my kin, but this is what I must do. I will be [ready] when you are.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Call'.\nYou say, 'ready'\nEssedera says, 'I admit that I find it impossible to wish you luck.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Sleeper's Tomb: The Call.\n\n---\n\n**Task Window Text:** The source of the restless ice may be hidden in the Sleeper's Tomb. If you can, find the source and stop it.\nYou say, 'Hail, a worried golem'\nA worried golem says, 'I will not blame you if you would like to [leave]. And if you foolishly wish to [retreat] back up into the tomb, I can assist you with that as well.'\nIf you say retreat, you will be teleported up a couple of levels, to the area where zone trash mobs are, to kill for instance collectibles, otherwise the main mission awaits on the 4 platforms ahead of you.\nYou say, 'Hail, Sivar'\nSivar says, 'You should leave this place. [What] goes on here now is not a matter for your kind. We have no quarrel with you, unless you [choose to interfere].'\nYou say, 'choose to interfere'\nSivar says, 'It is as we expected. Then you shall die!'\nA roar comes from the four corners of the room, each of different timbre, but all in large volume. - Event starts here\n1\\. Stop whatever is causing the restless ice. 0/1 The Sleeper's Tomb\n> **Task Window Text:** You sense a power at the heart of the Tomb. Find that power and shut it down.\nThe 4 Protector Dragons\nThese 4 Dragons can be fought in ANY order. The event allows time to meditate between dragon kills. The crystals will always activate in a clockwise rotation, starting at Melalafen's platform always, and progressing clockwise to yellow, then clear, then blue. This order always progresses in this fashion, even after dragons are slain. Doing so you can predict which Dragon's crystal aura will activate next. Each dragon must be fought on their platform or they will tether, summon, and strip your buffs.\nYour afflictions have been stripped.\nYour afflictions have been stripped.\nSivar begins casting Balance of the Nameless.\nCrystal Aura rotation order - Red, Yellow, Clear, Blue.\nThe central gem begins to glow. - 10 Second Warning\nThe crystal over the central platform glows and sends power into the red crystal. - Red Dragon goes inactive for 10 seconds, AE aura activates\nThese 2 emotes repeat for each of the 4 platforms, and always in a clockwise progression. The AEs that activate are as follows.\nReflected Fire \\- Red Gem/Melalafen's Platform\nReflected Sickness \\- Yellow Crystal/Honvar's Platform\nReflected Lightning \\- Clear Crystal/Sivar's Platform\nReflected Freeze \\- Blue Crystal/Cargalia's Platform\nEach AE has a 10% chance to apply an additional debuff of its own. However they are completely avoidable if you run out of the aura when the crystal activates, and the dragon goes inactive.\nMelalafen - Fire Dragon, Flame Resistant\nMelalafen rears back and flexes his wings - Right Wing Swing, Left Wing Swing. These can be avoided by staying in front or back of Melalafen.\nMelalafen takes a deep breath - Melalafen casts Velium Boosted Lava Breath, a frontal AE for 120320 dmg, but which also grants the players a Fire Infused Velium Shard [item=140312]\nMelalafen\nCargalia - Ice Dragon, Cold Resistant\nCargalia takes a deep breath - Cargalia casts Velium Boosted Frost Breath, a frontal AE for 120320 dmg, but which also grants the players a Frost Infused Velium Shard [item=140270]\nCargalia raises her tail - Tail Swing. This can be avoided by staying to the front or sides.\nSivar - Grey Dragon, Magic Resistant\nSivar roars a call to allies! - Summons A confused caretaker (gargoyle add)\nSivar takes a deep breath - Sivar casts Velium Boosted Lightning Breath, a frontal AE for 120320 dmg, but which also grants the players a Lightning Infused Velium Shard [item=140288]\nHonvar - Green Dragon, Poison/Disease Resistant\nHonvar takes a deep breath - Honvar casts Velium Boosted Chaos Breath, a frontal AE for 120320 dmg, but which alsos grants the players a Chaos Infused Velium Shard [item=140285]\nHonvar's claws scrape the ground - Claw Slash This can be avoided by staying to the sides or back.\nYou have time to meditate and recover mana between kills. However, once the fourth protector is slain, you must go DIRECTLY to Vulak Aerr in the center platform, or the event will reset after 30 seconds.\nAs the last guardian dragon falls, the barrier protecting the central platform fades away. - Engage Vulak Aerr in 30 seconds, or the event resets.\nVULAK`AERR - The Final Hurdle\nAt this point you must use all your burn abilities and kill Vulak`Aerr as quickly as possible. Thankfully he has far fewer HP than the previous 4 dragons. But Vulak has the same Wing and Tail AE's as Melalafen and Cargalia. Thankfully, if you are quick, he won't get to cast them much.\nPower flows out from the central gem to the smaller gems. Something forms under one of them.\nWhen you see this emote, time is running out, and several golems will start converging on the center from the 4 outer platforms. Kill him quickly, or the golems will reach the center and explode, each with a different AE.\nYou have slain Vulak`Aerr!\nEven though Vulak`Aerr is dead, you are still in danger from the golems that are converging at the center. Quickly, run underneath the central gem and touch it to de-activate the gem and spawn the Chest.\nThe magical device thrums loudly for a moment, and just stops spinning.\nThe moment you touch the device you sense a presence. All around this presence is the deepest cold, colder than you have ever imagined. The presence seems to be floating in pure silence. As you become aware of it, it becomes aware of you. As it begins to turn its attention to you a deep dread overcomes you and you pull away. The moment you flee the presence the device shuts down. Whatever that thing was, you know that it was beyond your comprehension.\nYour task 'The Call' has been updated.\n2\\. Open the chest and claim your reward. 0/1 The Sleeper's Tomb\nEven with the chest spawned, the golems will remain active, so quickly open the chest to despawn all the golems and auras permanently.\n_The restless ice will slowly fades [sic] now that the device is off. You hope._\nYour task 'The Call' has been updated.\nYou have received a replay timer for 'The Call': 0d:5h:8m remaining.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n177 platinum 8 silver 3 copper\nExperience\n45 Restless Marks\n**Submitted by:** Minasu\n- Restless Mark [item=140013]",
